Why this patch exists
---------------------
Tauri 2.12.1 always supplies a Wry navigation handler, including its plugin
wrapper when an application omits on_navigation. Wry's WebKitGTK callback then
settles every NavigationAction using only a URL and returns true, so a native
handler connected afterward cannot inspect the action or override that choice.
Linux receives iframe navigations through that same callback. URL-only handling
cannot distinguish automatically embedded frames from deliberate external links.

Small local difference
----------------------
Only src/lib.rs and src/webkitgtk/mod.rs differ from upstream:

* Export Linux-only set_webkit_policy_handler(&webkit2gtk::WebView, callback).
* Store one Rc callback in private per-view GObject data.
* Consult it before the existing decide-policy type switch. A true result stops
  fallback; false retains the original Wry/Tauri/plugin path exactly.
* Clone the Rc before calling user code, so callback replacement or re-entrant
  policy signals do not keep a borrowed qdata pointer alive.
* Export Linux-only set_webkit_new_window_handler(&webkit2gtk::WebView,
  callback), using a second private per-view Rc. Consult it before the existing
  create-signal URL handler; false denies creation, true retains the old path.
  WebKit may emit create without a preceding NewWindowAction policy decision,
  so the creation gate independently exposes the actual NavigationAction.

The hook is opt-in per native webview and GTK-thread only. Unregistered views,
including bundled controls, follow the original code. All non-Linux builds use
the original code. No navigation decision, opener, protocol permission, cookie
setting, user-agent change or IPC grant is added by this patch itself.
The hook is consulted by Wry's navigation-handler signal connection. Tauri
2.12.1 always supplies that connection through its plugin wrapper; a raw Wry
view built without a navigation handler does not consult the installed hook.
The new-window gate similarly requires Wry's new-window-handler connection;
Tauri app views that register on_new_window supply it. Without a registered
native creation gate, the original create path is unchanged.

The callback must return true if it calls use/ignore/download; only WebKit's
first decision has effect. It must return false without settling the decision
when normal Wry/Tauri/plugin handling is wanted. Callers install it while the
view is neutral, before its first remote load or before returning a related
popup from NewWindowResponse::Create. Do not capture a strong reference to the
same view in its stored callback. The callback is released with the native view
or on replacement. This API does not add reliable pre-request frame identity.

Maintenance and validation
--------------------------
Keep the complete upstream license and package baseline when updating. Compare
these two source files with the new pinned release and re-check Tauri's wrapper
and Wry signal order before carrying the patch forward. Prefer an upstream
native policy hook when available; do not apply an unrelated version upgrade
silently. The package-level patch must be exercised through the app's native
frame/popup tests (handled=true, fallback=false, unhooked controls, callback
replacement/re-entry, auth redirects, iframe/main response classification and
related opener/postMessage/close behavior). A successful Rust build alone does
not establish correct routing or compatibility with real service previews.
The creation-gate checks must include create-only JavaScript popups whose
NavigationType is Other even when recent user activation makes is_user_gesture
true; gesture alone must not be mistaken for a deliberate clicked link.
